course: dictionary
lesson: 15606
title: Tanned
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «After two weeks on the beach, Maya came home with tanned arms and a brown nose.» Tanned means her skin has gone darker because it was in the sun. The clues are beach and sun, so the word is about sunlight changing skin.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «After two weeks in the sun, Maya came home with darker skin.» It still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: The same word can mean something different. «The tanned leather boots were stiff and brown.» Here tanned means animal skin that has been made into leather with a special treatment. The clues are leather and boots, not sunshine, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: A tan is the skin's reaction to sun, and too much sun can burn and harm skin. That is why we use sun cream and wear a hat.
fact: Tanned means having darker skin after time in the sun.
fact: «Sun-tanned» means tanned by the sun, like a holiday glow.
fact: A tan is the skin's reaction to sun, and too much sun can burn and harm skin.
fact: Tanned leather is animal skin that has been made into leather by a special treatment.
fact: A tanner is a person who makes leather from animal skin.
exercise: «After two weeks on the beach, Maya had tanned arms.» What does tanned mean here? | Cold and wet from the sea | Covered in sand | *Darker skin from the sun | Sore from a fall
exercise: «The tanned leather boots were stiff and brown.» What has been tanned here? | A wooden table | The sky at sunset | The children's faces | *Animal skin, made into leather
exercise: «Too much sun can burn your skin.» What should you use to protect your skin? | Nothing, because a tan is always safe | Ice cubes rubbed on your arms | *Sun cream and a hat | Sunbathing from noon until dark
test: «Dad came back from the desert with sun-tanned skin.» What does sun-tanned mean? | Painted gold | *Darker skin, made by the sun | Sore and red, like a burn | Dressed in warm clothes
test: Which word means nearly the same as tanned in «His arms were tanned from the summer sun»? | Wrinkled | *Browned by the sun | Frozen | Painted blue
exam: «The tanner worked all day, turning cow hides into tanned leather.» What is a tanner? | A person who swims in the sea | *A person who makes leather from animal skin | A kind of sun cream | A holiday in the sun
